From e84d3e8fc4b12b7409bc0e6d9580c68f89470f0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JuggyMcNutty <11588877+JuggyMcNutty@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 17:03:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Gamepad support, and two Deus Ex script-interop fixes

FORK ONLY. This project ships a NO-AI Code Rule asking that LLM-written
changes stay in a fork and are never PR'd upstream. These were written with
Claude. Do not submit them.

Controller support for a handheld with no mouse or keyboard:

- SurrealWidgets: GamepadState plus two DisplayBackend virtuals with no-op
  defaults, GetGamepadState() and SetGamepadKeyEmulation(). The SDL2
  backend polls the first attached controller (reopening after an unplug)
  and, when emulation is off, drops the controller button events it used to
  turn into Enter/Escape/arrow keys, so buttons do not arrive twice.
  Polling keeps the change out of Widget's focus dispatch.
- GamepadInput, called from Engine::UpdateInput: in play, buttons are the UE1
  joystick keys (A=Joy1 ... START=Joy8, digital L2/R2=Joy11/Joy12 past half
  travel, d-pad=JoyPov*) and sticks/triggers are JoyX/Y/U/V/Z/R axis events
  (+-100 at full, up positive, radial dead zone, a curve on the look stick),
  so User.ini bindings decide what they do. While a Deus Ex modal window is
  open, a stick moves the pointer, A/X click, B/Y/SELECT/START are Escape,
  the d-pad is the arrow keys and L1/R1 scroll. Releases go to whichever
  side saw the press. PollSkip() lets the pad skip movies.
- LauncherSettings gains a Gamepad block (Enabled, DeadZone, look speeds,
  InvertY, CursorSpeed, Layout); absent members keep their defaults and
  Save() writes it back. Enabled=false restores the old key emulation.

Deus Ex fixes:

- CycleActors (native 1002) is resumable: ScriptedPawn.CheckEnemyPresence
  keeps CycleIndex between ticks, checks ~20 candidates a tick and reads
  "index went down" as a full lap. The iterator ignored the incoming index
  and rebuilt a list of every matching actor with a name-based IsA on each
  call, so it was the costliest native on Liberty Island (~0.66 ms a call,
  ~46 calls a frame) and each NPC only ever considered the first ~21 pawns.
  It now continues after Index, wraps, stops after one lap, and compares
  class pointers along BaseStruct.
- DeusExPlayer.ShowMainMenu sets the travel variable bIgnoreNextShowMenu
  when Escape skips the intro, to swallow a duplicate event the original
  engine delivered. Surreal delivers one, so the flag ate the player's first
  attempt to open the pause menu in the next level. LoginPlayer and
  PossessSavedPlayer now clear it (Deus Ex only).

Verified on the TrimUI Smart Pro: move, look and fire from the pad (first
build); the CycleActors change removed that native from the profile and
kept the scan behaviour the script expects. The pause-menu fix and the
menu-mode button changes are built and deployed but not yet tried by hand.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
